{"timestamp":"2026-09-16T14:42:50.188Z","ordinal":862,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0aaab-a2cc-78f2-bfd5-1383e0721b10","call_id":"call_EDhYUCz0HvmDcGPN1cZlvmNR","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"47a50b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004704,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6019,\"output\":\" M docs/OFFLINE_GUIDE.md\\n M docs/SERVING_GUIDE.md\\n M scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh\\n M scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh\\n M tests/test_kv_load_metrics.py\\n M tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/__init__.py\\n M tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/frozen_split.py\\n M tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/init.py\\n M tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/kv.py\\n M tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/timing.py\\n M tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/weights.py\\n M tiered_serve/graph_wait_ops.py\\n M tiered_serve/immigrant_model_loader.py\\n M tiered_serve/kv_load_metrics.py\\n M tiered_serve/torch_hooks.py\\n M tiered_serve/v1_cuda_graph_wrapper.py\\n?? docs/BREAKDOWN_GUIDE.md\\n?? etc/stack_pool_diag.c\\n?? etc/stack_pool_diag.so\\n?? scripts/summarize_breakdown_intervals.py\\n?? tests/test_breakdown_intervals.py\\n?? tiered_serve/breakdown_intervals.py\\n?? tiered_serve/breakdown_markers.py\\n?? tiered_serve/breakdown_output.py\\n?? tiered_serve/breakdown_worker.py\\nf4ab632457015f416d7d09ebde83f284d6062582\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Bounded, nonblocking handoff of numeric snapshots to a CPU-only process.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport atexit\\nimport json\\nimport logging\\nimport queue\\nimport struct\\nimport subprocess\\nimport sys\\nimport threading\\nimport time\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom multiprocessing.util import Finalize\\n\\nimport msgspec\\n\\n\\nclass AsyncBreakdownWriter:\\n    def __init__(self, directory, suffix, capacity=64):\\n        self.directory = Path(directory)\\n        self.directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n        self.suffix = suffix\\n        self.pending = queue.Queue(maxsize=capacity)\\n        self.attempted = self.submitted = self.dropped = 0\\n        self.enqueue_cpu_ms = 0.0\\n        self.error = None\\n        self.closed = False\\n        self.before_close = None\\n        # No torch import, forked CUDA context, or inherited serving SIGINT.\\n        # EOF shuts down the child even if its parent is killed unexpectedly.\\n        worker = Path(__file__).with_name(\\\"breakdown_worker.py\\\")\\n        self.process = subprocess.Popen(\\n            [sys.executable, str(worker), str(self.directory), suffix],\\n            stdin=subprocess.PIPE, start_new_session=True)\\n        self.thread = threading.Thread(target=self._send, daemon=True,\\n                                       name=\\\"breakdown-output\\\")\\n        self.thread.start()\\n        atexit.register(self.close)\\n        self.finalizer = Finalize(None, self.close, exitpriority=10)\\n\\n    def submit(self, frame):\\n        self.attempted += 1\\n        if self.error is not None or self.closed:\\n            self.dropped += 1\\n            return\\n        started = time.perf_counter()\\n        # Serialize outside the next GPU forward. The transport thread only\\n        # does blocking pipe I/O (which releases the GIL), never analysis.\\n        data = msgspec.msgpack.encode(frame)\\n        try:\\n            self.pending.put_nowait(data)\\n            self.submitted += 1\\n        except queue.Full:\\n            self.dropped += 1\\n            self.error = \\\"breakdown output backlog exceeded capacity\\\"\\n            logging.getLogger(\\\"vllm\\\").error(\\\"%s; diagnostic run is incomplete\\\", self.error)\\n        self.enqueue_cpu_ms += (time.perf_counter() - started) * 1000\\n\\n    def _send(self):\\n        try:\\n            while True:\\n                data = self.pending.get()\\n                if data is None:\\n                    break\\n                self.process.stdin.write(struct.pack(\\\"!Q\\\", len(data)))\\n                self.process.stdin.write(data)\\n            self.process.stdin.flush()\\n        except (BrokenPipeError, OSError) as error:\\n            self.error = str(error)\\n        finally:\\n            self.process.stdin.close()\\n\\n    def close(self):\\n        if self.closed:\\n            return\\n        # Only shutdown may drain outstanding work and wait for disk I/O.\\n        # The model owner uses this to read the final logits events.\\n        if self.before_close is not None:\\n            self.before_close()\\n        self.closed = True\\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + 60\\n        trailer = msgspec.msgpack.encode(dict(finish=True, expected=self.submitted))\\n        for item in (trailer, None):\\n            while self.thread.is_alive():\\n                try:\\n                    self.pending.put(item, timeout=0.1)\\n                    break\\n                except queue.Full:\\n                    if time.monotonic() >= deadline:\\n                        self.error = \\\"breakdown shutdown drain timed out\\\"\\n                        break\\n        self.thread.join(timeout=max(0, deadline - time.monotonic()))\\n        try:\\n            self.process.wait(timeout=max(0.1, deadline - time.monotonic()))\\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\\n            self.process.terminate()\\n            self.process.wait(timeout=5)\\n            self.error = \\\"breakdown worker shutdown timed out\\\"\\n        status = dict(\\n            attempted=self.attempted, submitted=self.submitted, dropped=self.dropped,\\n            enqueue_cpu_ms=self.enqueue_cpu_ms, worker_exit=self.process.returncode,\\n            error=self.error, complete=not self.error and not self.dropped\\n            and self.process.returncode == 0)\\n        path = self.directory / f\\\"breakdown_capture.{self.suffix}.json\\\"\\n        path.write_text(json.dumps(status, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Spool snapshots while inference runs; CPU analysis happens after the run.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport struct\\nimport sys\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport msgspec\\n\\n\\nMAGIC = b\\\"TSBD1\\\\x00\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef read_exact(stream, size):\\n    parts = []\\n    while size:\\n        data = stream.read(size)\\n        if not data:\\n            raise EOFError(\\\"incomplete breakdown frame\\\")\\n        parts.append(data)\\n        size -= len(data)\\n    return b\\\"\\\".join(parts)\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    directory, suffix = Path(sys.argv[1]), sys.argv[2]\\n    status_path = directory / f\\\"breakdown_status.{suffix}.json\\\"\\n    status = dict(complete=False, forwards=0, error=None)\\n    status_path.write_text(json.dumps(status))\\n    spool = open(directory / f\\\"breakdown_snapshots.{suffix}.msgpack\\\", \\\"wb\\\")\\n    spool.write(MAGIC)\\n    try:\\n        while True:\\n            header = sys.stdin.buffer.read(8)\\n            if not header:\\n                raise EOFError(\\\"producer exited without a completed drain\\\")\\n            if len(header) < 8:\\n                header += read_exact(sys.stdin.buffer, 8 - len(header))\\n            length, = struct.unpack(\\\"!Q\\\", header)\\n            data = read_exact(sys.stdin.buffer, length)\\n            frame = msgspec.msgpack.decode(data)\\n            if frame.get(\\\"finish\\\"):\\n                if frame[\\\"expected\\\"] != status[\\\"forwards\\\"]:\\n                    raise ValueError(\\\"breakdown frame count mismatch\\\")\\n                status[\\\"complete\\\"] = True\\n                break\\n            spool.write(header)\\n            spool.write(data)\\n            status[\\\"forwards\\\"] += 1\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        status[\\\"error\\\"] = str(error)\\n    finally:\\n        spool.close()\\n        temporary = status_path.with_suffix(\\\".tmp\\\")\\n        temporary.write_text(json.dumps(status, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n        temporary.replace(status_path)\\n    return 0 if status[\\\"complete\\\"] else 1\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    sys.exit(main())\\n                \\\"gpu_fwd_ms\\\": total_time,\\n                \\\"compute_ms\\\": llm_brk,\\n                \\\"dense_compute_ms\\\": dense_compute_brk,\\n                \\\"fused_weight_compute_ms\\\": fused_weight_compute_brk,\\n                \\\"productive_compute_ms\\\": productive_compute_brk,\\n                \\\"exec_residual_ms\\\": exec_residual_brk,\\n                \\\"wdecomp_ms\\\": wdecomp_brk,\\n                \\\"kvdecomp_ms\\\": kvdecomp_brk,\\n                \\\"wload_ms\\\": wload_brk,\\n                \\\"kvload_ms\\\": kvload_brk,\\n                \\\"kv_load_residual_estimate_ms\\\": kv_load_residual,\\n                **{key: kv_metrics[key] for key in (\\n                    \\\"kv_raw_bytes\\\", \\\"kv_payload_bytes\\\", \\\"kv_h2d_bytes\\\",\\n                    \\\"kv_compression_ratio\\\", \\\"kv_transfer_ratio\\\")},\\n                \\\"stall_ms\\\": stall_brk,\\n                \\\"exposed_load_ms\\\": exposed_load_brk,\\n                \\\"unclassified_ms\\\": unclassified_brk,\\n                \\\"compute_markers\\\": len(kernel_intervals),\\n                \\\"compute_markers_expected\\\": expected_compute_markers,\\n                \\\"fused_override_markers\\\": len(fused_override_entries),\\n                \\\"fused_kernel_markers\\\": len(actual_fused_event_ids),\\n                \\\"fused_fallback_markers\\\": len(fallback_dense_event_ids),\\n                \\\"raw_prefill_dense_markers\\\": len(\\n                    raw_prefill_dense_event_ids),\\n                \\\"window_clip_count\\\": self._timing_window_clip_count,\\n                \\\"window_drop_count\\\": self._timing_window_drop_count,\\n                \\\"instrumented\\\": True,\\n                \\\"compute_includes_weight_decomp\\\": False,\\n                \\\"fused_weight_compute_includes_weight_decomp\\\": bool(\\n                    actual_fused_event_ids),\\n                \\\"wload_measurement\\\": \\\"direct_union\\\",\\n                \\\"kvload_measurement\\\": \\\"h2d_submission_window_sum\\\",\\n            }\\n            capture_started = perf_counter()\\n            intervals = self._layer_intervals(\\n                init_event, total_time, transfers, actual_fused_event_ids,\\n                fallback_dense_event_ids)\\n            frame = dict(\\n                context=kv_metrics, intervals=intervals, total_ms=total_time,\\n                complete=compute_markers_valid and bool(kv_metrics[\\\"timing_complete\\\"]),\\n                prefetch_issues=self._prefetch_issue_times(),\\n                capture_cpu_ms=(perf_counter() - capture_started) * 1000)\\n            # Numeric snapshots survive event reuse; retain only this forward's\\n            # start event from a two-slot pool until its separate logits is read.\\n            self._pending_breakdown = (init_event, frame)\\n            self._pending_logits_recorded = False\\n            self._breakdown_collecting = False\\n            if (not self.batch_has_prefill and use_kv_comp\\n                    and getattr(_kc, \\\"_cpu_profile_enabled\\\", False)):\\n                _join_total = float(getattr(\\n                    _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_join_total_ms\\\", 0.0))\\n                _worker_wait = float(getattr(\\n                    _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_worker_wait_ms\\\", 0.0))\\n                self.last_breakdown.update({\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_join_ms\\\": _join_total,\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_worker_wait_ms\\\": _worker_wait,\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_publish_ms\\\": max(\\n                        0.0, _join_total - _worker_wait),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_join_calls\\\": int(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_join_calls\\\", 0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_join_blocks\\\": int(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_join_blocks\\\", 0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_join_max_ms\\\": float(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_join_max_ms\\\", 0.0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_fast_commit_ms\\\": float(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_fast_commit_ms\\\", 0.0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_fast_finalize_ms\\\": float(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_fast_finalize_ms\\\", 0.0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_legacy_get_ms\\\": float(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_legacy_get_ms\\\", 0.0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_legacy_finalize_ms\\\": float(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_legacy_finalize_ms\\\", 0.0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_fast_candidates\\\": int(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_fast_candidates\\\", 0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_fast_hits\\\": int(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_fast_hits\\\", 0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_fast_fallbacks\\\": int(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_fast_fallbacks\\\", 0)),\\n                    \\\"kv_cpu_raw_blocks\\\": int(getattr(\\n                        _kc, \\\"_step_cpu_raw_blocks\\\", 0)),\\n                })\\n            if self.batch_has_prefill:\\n                DualMemoryLoader.prefill_breakdowns.append(self.last_breakdown)\\n            else:\\n                # Stash the per-component stall/load arrays computed in the\\n                # decode stall block above so the driver can print one\\n                # batch-averaged BarrierWait / ComponentLoad line.\\n                self.last_breakdown[\\\"comp_stall\\\"] = list(comp_stall)\\n                self.last_breakdown[\\\"attn_barrier_wait\\\"] = attn_barrier_wait\\n                self.last_breakdown[\\\"weight_stall\\\"] = weight_stall\\n                self.last_breakdown[\\\"comp_load\\\"] = list(comp_load)\\n                self.last_breakdown[\\\"kv_load_ms\\\"] = kv_load_ms\\n                DualMemoryLoader.decode_breakdowns.append(self.last_breakdown)\\n\\n        self.reset_events()\\n\\n    def _layer_intervals(self, origin, total_ms, transfers, fused_ids,\\n                         fallback_ids):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Read the existing event pools before reset, retaining their owners.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        rows = []\\n        components = (\\\"qkv\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"gate_up\\\", \\\"down\\\")\\n        kernel_slots = (0, 1, 3, 4)\\n\\n        def add(layer, activity, component, source, begin, end):\\n            if activity == \\\"WAIT\\\":\\n                # Successful prefetch can have a sub-microsecond wait. Keep\\n                # those markers as NeedTime too, including zero-length pairs.\\n                try:\\n                    start, stop = self._event_offset(origin, begin), self._event_offset(origin, end)\\n                except RuntimeError:\\n                    return\\n                pairs = [(start, stop)] if 0 <= start <= stop <= total_ms else []\\n            else:\\n                pair_key = (id(begin), id(end), activity == \\\"PRODUCTIVE\\\")\\n                cached = getattr(self, \\\"_timing_interval_pairs\\\", {})\\n                if pair_key in cached:\\n                    pair = cached[pair_key]\\n                    pairs = [pair] if pair is not None else []\\n                else:\\n                    pairs = self._calc_intervals(\\n                        origin, [begin], [end], total_ms,\\n                        require_contained=activity == \\\"PRODUCTIVE\\\", count_invalid=False)\\n            if source == \\\"dense_fallback\\\":\\n                # Subtract only this projection's fallback decode. Another\\n                # layer's concurrent decode must not erase its dense GEMM.\\n                entry = self._fused_reg[4 * layer + components.index(component)]\\n                fallback = self._calc_intervals(\\n                    origin, [entry[8]], [entry[9]], total_ms,\\n                    require_contained=True, count_invalid=False)\\n                pairs = self._subtract_intervals(pairs, fallback)\\n            for start, stop in pairs:\\n                rows.append(dict(layer=layer, activity=activity, component=component,\\n                                 source=source, begin_ms=start, end_ms=stop))\\n\\n        for index, (begin, end) in enumerate(zip(\\n                self.begin_kernel_events, self.end_kernel_events)):\\n            source = (\\\"fused_weight_compute\\\" if index in fused_ids else\\n                      \\\"dense_fallback\\\" if index in fallback_ids else \\\"dense_compute\\\")\\n            add(index // 5, \\\"PRODUCTIVE\\\",\\n                (\\\"qkv\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"attention\\\", \\\"gate_up\\\", \\\"down\\\")[index % 5],\\n                source, begin, end)\\n        if getattr(self, \\\"aux_timing_enabled\\\", False):\\n            for component, begin, end in zip(\\n                    (\\\"embed\\\", \\\"final_norm\\\"),\\n                    self.begin_aux_compute_events[:2], self.end_aux_compute_events[:2]):\\n                add(-1, \\\"PRODUCTIVE\\\", component, \\\"aux_compute\\\", begin, end)\\n\\n        for activity, begins, ends, source in (\\n                (\\\"LOAD\\\", self.begin_memcpy_weight_events,\\n                 self.end_memcpy_weight_events, \\\"weight_h2d\\\"),\\n                (\\\"WDECOMP\\\", self.begin_decomp_events,\\n                 self.end_decomp_events, \\\"weight_decode\\\"),\\n                (\\\"WAIT\\\", self._v1_wwait_begin_events,\\n                 self._v1_wwait_end_events, \\\"weight_wait\\\")):\\n            if activity == \\\"WDECOMP\\\" and not (\\n                    DualMemoryLoader.use_weight_comp and DualMemoryLoader.load_comp_weight):\\n                continue\\n            for index, (begin, end) in enumerate(zip(begins, ends)):\\n                if activity != \\\"WAIT\\\" and index // 4 not in self.not_frozen_layers:\\n                    continue\\n                add(index // 4, activity, components[index % 4], source, begin, end)\\n\\n        if DualMemoryLoader.use_weight_comp:\\n            for component_id, component in enumerate(components):\\n                begins = getattr(self, \\\"begin_frozen_decomp_events\\\", {}).get(component, [])\\n                ends = getattr(self, \\\"end_frozen_decomp_timing_events\\\", {}).get(component, [])\\n                for layer, (begin, end) in enumerate(zip(begins, ends)):\\n                    source = (\\\"fused_fallback\\\" if 5 * layer + kernel_slots[component_id]\\n                              in fallback_ids else \\\"frozen_weight_decode\\\")\\n                    add(layer, \\\"WDECOMP\\\", component, source, begin, end)\\n\\n        for activity, begin_attr, end_attr, source in (\\n                (\\\"LOAD\\\", \\\"_frozen_split_h2d_begin_events_cache\\\",\\n                 \\\"_frozen_split_h2d_end_timing_events_cache\\\", \\\"split_weight_h2d\\\"),\\n                (\\\"WDECOMP\\\", \\\"_frozen_split_decomp_begin_timing_events_cache\\\",\\n                 \\\"_frozen_split_decomp_end_timing_events_cache\\\", \\\"split_weight_decode\\\")):\\n            begins, ends = getattr(self, begin_attr, {}), getattr(self, end_attr, {})\\n            for key in begins.keys() & ends.keys():\\n                layer, name = key[:2]\\n                component = next((comp for comp in components if f\\\"{comp}_proj\\\" in name),\\n                                 \\\"unknown\\\")\\n                add(layer, activity, component, source, begins[key], ends[key])\\n\\n        for item in transfers:\\n            if item.events is not None:\\n                add(item.layer, \\\"LOAD\\\", \\\"kv\\\", \\\"kv_h2d_submission\\\", *item.events)\\n        if DualMemoryLoader.use_kv_comp:\\n            compressor = getattr(self, \\\"kv_compressor\\\", None)\\n            begins = getattr(compressor, \\\"_kv_decode_begin\\\", None)\\n            if begins is None or len(begins) != len(self.end_kv_decomp_events):\\n                begins = getattr(compressor, \\\"_kv_dec_h2d\\\", None)\\n            if begins is None or len(begins) != len(self.end_kv_decomp_events):\\n                begins = self.begin_kv_decomp_events\\n            for layer, (begin, end) in enumerate(zip(begins, self.end_kv_decomp_events)):\\n                add(layer, \\\"KVDECOMP\\\", \\\"kv\\\", \\\"kv_decode\\\", begin, end)\\n        for layer, (begin, end) in enumerate(zip(\\n                self._v1_kv_wait_begin_events, self._v1_kv_wait_end_events)):\\n            if layer < self.n_layers:\\n                add(layer, \\\"WAIT\\\", \\\"kv\\\", \\\"kv_wait\\\", begin, end)\\n        ready_events = dict(getattr(self, \\\"weight_wait_events\\\", {}))\\n        ready_events.update({(layer, \\\"kv\\\"): event for layer, event in enumerate(\\n            getattr(self, \\\"exec_attn_barriers\\\", ()))})\\n        ready_owners = Counter(id(event) for event in ready_events.values() if event is not None)\\n        for (layer, component), event in ready_events.items():\\n            if event is None or ready_owners[id(event)] != 1:\\n                continue\\n            issue = getattr(self, \\\"prefetch_issue_host_ms\\\", {}).get((layer, component))\\n            if issue is not None and issue[2] > 1:\\n                # A reused readiness slot cannot identify which submission the\\n                # consumer waited on. Do not silently attribute the last one.\\n                continue\\n            try:\\n                ready = self._event_offset(origin, event)\\n            except RuntimeError:\\n                continue\\n            rows.append(dict(layer=layer, activity=\\\"READY\\\", component=component,\\n                             source=\\\"consumer_wait_event\\\", begin_ms=ready, end_ms=ready))\\n        return rows\\n\\n    def record_prefetch_issue(self, layer, component):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"CPU scheduling entry on a host clock, with no GPU marker or dependency.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not self._breakdown_collecting:\\n            return\\n        key = (layer, component)\\n        now = (perf_counter() - self._forward_host_start) * 1000\\n        previous = self.prefetch_issue_host_ms.get(key)\\n        if previous is None:\\n            self.prefetch_issue_host_ms[key] = (now, now, 1)\\n        else:\\n            self.prefetch_issue_host_ms[key] = (previous[0], now, previous[2] + 1)\\n\\n    def _prefetch_issue_times(self):\\n        return [dict(layer=layer, component=component, first_issue_host_ms=first,\\n                     last_issue_host_ms=last, issue_count=count)\\n                for (layer, component), (first, last, count)\\n                in self.prefetch_issue_host_ms.items()]\\n\\n    def _flush_pending_breakdown(self, final=False):\\n        pending = self._pending_breakdown\\n        if pending is None:\\n            return\\n        origin, frame = pending\\n        if self._pending_logits_recorded:\\n            if final:\\n                # Shutdown only; the inference path never waits for these\\n                # extra markers or widens the old synchronization scope.\\n                self.end_logits_event.synchronize()\\n            if self.end_logits_event.query():\\n                begin = origin.elapsed_time(self.begin_aux_compute_events[2])\\n                end = origin.elapsed_time(self.end_aux_compute_events[2])\\n                if frame[\\\"total_ms\\\"] <= begin <= end:\\n                    frame[\\\"post_model\\\"] = dict(\\n                        lm_head_ms=end - begin,\\n                        logits_span_ms=self.begin_aux_compute_events[2].elapsed_time(\\n                            self.end_logits_event),\\n                        intervals=[dict(layer=-1, activity=\\\"PRODUCTIVE\\\", component=\\\"lm_head\\\",\\n                                        source=\\\"aux_compute\\\", begin_ms=begin, end_ms=end)])\\n        self.breakdown_writer.submit(frame)\\n        self._pending_breakdown = None\\n        self._pending_logits_recorded = False\\n\\n    def _event_offset(self, origin, event):\\n        # Each CUDA timestamp is read once per model snapshot, then shared by\\n        # legacy aggregates and detailed attribution. No extra CUDA records.\\n        cache = getattr(self, \\\"_timing_offsets\\\", None)\\n        if cache is None:\\n            return origin.elapsed_time(event)\\n        key = (id(origin), id(event))\\n        if key not in cache:\\n            cache[key] = origin.elapsed_time(event)\\n        return cache[key]\\n\\n    def _subtract_intervals(\\n        self,\\n        intervals_a: List[Tuple[float, float]],\\n        intervals_b: List[Tuple[float, float]],\\n    ) -> List[Tuple[float, float]]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return ``intervals_a`` minus ``intervals_b`` as a sorted,\\n        non-overlapping list.  Both inputs must already be sorted by\\n        start time and individually non-overlapping (same precondition\\n        as :func:`_calculate_total_overlap`).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not intervals_b:\\n            return [(s, e) for s, e in intervals_a]\\n        result: List[Tuple[float, float]] = []\\n        bi = 0\\n        for a_start, a_end in intervals_a:\\n            cur = a_start\\n            # Advance bi past intervals strictly before cur.\\n            while bi < len(intervals_b) and intervals_b[bi][1] <= cur:\\n                bi += 1\\n            j = bi\\n            while cur < a_end and j < len(intervals_b):\\n                b_start, b_end = intervals_b[j]\\n                if b_start >= a_end:\\n                    break\\n                if b_start > cur:\\n                    result.append((cur, min(b_start, a_end)))\\n                cur = max(cur, b_end)\\n                j += 1\\n            if cur < a_end:\\n                result.append((cur, a_end))\\n        return result\\n\\n    def _calculate_total_overlap(\\n        self,\\n        intervals_a: List[Tuple[float, float]],\\n        intervals_b: List[Tuple[float, float]],\\n    ) -> float:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        두 개의 시간 간격 리스트가 겹치는 총 시간을 효율적으로 계산합니다.\\n        (각 리스트는 내부적으로 겹치지 않고 정렬되어 있다고 가정합니다.)\\n\\n        Args:\\n            intervals_a: 첫 번째 시간 간격 리스트\\n            intervals_b: 두 번째 시간 간격 리스트\\n\\n        Returns:\\n            두 리스트가 겹치는 총 시간 (float)\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # 두 리스트가 시작 시간 기준으로 정렬되어 있어야 합니다.\\n\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"047266\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002816,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1198,\"output\":\"---\\nname: implement\\ndescription: Implement an accepted feature, PRD, issue, or concrete set of requirements through relevant verification and review. Use when the user requests implementation of agreed behavior. Simple localized edits can be handled directly; questions, research, and design-only requests do not start this workflow.\\n---\\n\\nScale this workflow to the accepted work. A small localized edit does not need a separate review workflow or commit merely because this skill is available. Automatic selection does not grant additional authorization.\\n\\nImplement the accepted work described by the user, PRD, or issues. Record the starting working-tree state and task file scope so unrelated changes remain separate.\\n\\nUse `tdd` for explicit test-first requests and behavior where regression coverage is useful. Reuse agreed or obvious existing interfaces; ask only about material unresolved contracts. Complete each slice through the accepted intended flow.\\n\\nRun affected tests, relevant type checks, and repository-required checks. Run the full suite when change reach, risk, failures, or unresolved concerns warrant it; do not repeat passing checks without a reason.\\n\\nUse [verification evidence](../code-review/references/verification-evidence.md) when recording checks, deciding whether a previous result remains applicable, or retrying a partially completed batch.\\n\\nFor substantive implementation changes or an explicit review request, use `code-review` before committing on the actual in-scope staged, unstaged, and untracked changes, with the accepted requirements and starting baseline. Correct actionable findings and rerun affected verification.\\n\\nCommit only this task's work to the current branch when the user's instructions permit committing. Honor requests to leave changes uncommitted. A local commit does not authorize pushing, publishing, or deployment.\\n---\\nname: diagnosing-bugs\\ndescription: Diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Use for unclear, intermittent, or difficult bugs and performance regressions, or when the user asks for a structured diagnosis.\\n---\\n\\n# Diagnosing hard bugs\\n\\nUse this loop for unclear, intermittent, or difficult bugs and performance regressions. A localized fix with clear evidence can use a shorter loop. Read relevant domain vocabulary and architectural decisions when present.\\n\\n## Establish the observed failure\\n\\nRecord the expected outcome, actual outcome, environment, and intended entry point. Use existing UI behavior, logs, traces, or a user report as evidence; distinguish observation from inference. Improve reproducibility while inspecting relevant code and forming hypotheses. A deterministic command is useful, but is not a prerequisite for reasoning or independent progress.\\n\\nChoose the closest practical existing interface that preserves the real control flow. A focused test, CLI command, browser interaction, or recorded trace can tighten feedback. Mocks and harnesses can isolate a cause but cannot prove the requested capability works. The optional `scripts/hitl-loop.template.sh` is a helper for suitable shell environments, not a required runtime.\\n\\n## Narrow and explain\\n\\nReduce the failing case enough to discriminate plausible causes without losing the original behavior. Rank hypotheses against evidence; test the most informative ones. Share material findings without waiting for approval of routine diagnostic steps. For intermittent failures, choose repetitions and measurements appropriate to the observed rate and cost, and report the uncertainty rather than imposing a universal threshold.\\n\\nIf access or evidence is missing, state exactly what cannot be verified and request the smallest missing input. Continue code inspection and other independent investigation. Do not claim a fix on the strength of an unverified hypothesis.\\n\\n## Fix and verify\\n\\nWhen implementation is authorized, make the smallest complete correction that preserves the accepted architecture and outcome. Add the smallest meaningful regression test reproducing the failure at an appropriate existing interface; establish that it fails for the original defect when practical. If automated reproduction is unavailable, retain direct failure evidence and state the coverage limitation.\\n\\nUse [verification evidence](../code-review/references/verification-evidence.md) for retries and result freshness. Retain the original failure and distinguish a failing check from a check that never ran.\\n\\nVerify the same representative flow again, then run affected and repository-required checks. Remove temporary instrumentation introduced for diagnosis. Explain the cause, change, evidence, and remaining limits. Report any broader architectural opportunity separately; do not expand this fix into a redesign without authorization.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0aaab-655f-73e1-915a-d9985ed7468b","create_time":1789569770.1883705}}}
